    "status": "OK",
    "chars": 3077,
    "grade": "PASS",
    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In a previous post , we introduced TorchNeuron, the native PyTorch backend for AWS Trainium (the torch-neuronx package).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With it, Transformers runs its own modeling code on Trainium, as it does on any other device, so any Transformers model on the Hub may run.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It tells you whether a model runs unmodified on Trainium, and gives you the script to run it yourself.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Each row gives the result, the number of Trainium cores the model is sharded over, the wall time of the run (compilation included) and the peak device memory.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To look up a given model, switch to the Trending or Downloads view and type part of its name.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On a Trainium2 ( trn2 ) instance with that stack, for example in the AWS Neuron Deep Learning Container , install the packages, then run:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A first run starts by compiling the model's graphs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Each test loads the model on a trn2 instance, sharded over the smallest number of Trainium cores that can hold its weights.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The test then generates 32 tokens and checks them.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When the model is sharded, a small judge model checks that the text is fluent English.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "At the time of writing, only models that fit on 4 Trainium2 devices are tested, which means 16 cores at most.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Next time you wonder whether a model runs on Trainium, look it up .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/torch-neuronx-model-support",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T15:00:46.512Z"
      }
    ],
